// Six vehicles park at once in a car park of two aisles
// (examples/parking/check/carpark.ent, parking-SPEC.md scene 13): each
// with Tesla's cameras, their errors on, a belief grid, a search and a
// parker of its own (rows of its own of the buffers, by windows), and
// the vehicles of an aisle are things to each other. All park and none
// touches anything; on one core and with every loop over the vehicles
// on six threads, the same lines.
// RUN: %ent run -I %S/../../examples/parking %S/../../examples/parking/check/carpark.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.one
// RUN: env ENT_PARALLEL_MIN=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=6 %ent run --parallel -I %S/../../examples/parking %S/../../examples/parking/check/carpark.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.all
// RUN: diff %t.one %t.all
// RUN: FileCheck %s --input-file=%t.one

// CHECK: vehicle 1 (Tesla Model 3 (2024)): Done, parked true, touched 0,
// CHECK: vehicle 2 (Tesla Model 3 (2017-2023)): Done, parked true, touched 0,
// CHECK: vehicle 3 (smart fortwo): Done, parked true, touched 0,
// CHECK: vehicle 4 (Tesla Model 3 (2024)): Done, parked true, touched 0,
// CHECK: vehicle 5 (Tesla Model 3 (2017-2023)): Done, parked true, touched 0,
// CHECK: vehicle 6 (smart fortwo): Done, parked true, touched 0,
